    "/repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{issue_number}/references": {
      "get": {
        "description": "Fyrden (GitHub shows these as cross-referenced events in its timeline): the issues, pull requests and comments whose text names this issue or pull request (\`#12\`, or \`owner/repo#12\` from another repository), by repository, then number. A reference shows only when the caller can read both its ends: this issue or pull request with its kind's permission, and the source's repository with the source's kind's permission; one whose repository is gone is left out. A page holds only references the caller sees, and checks at most 10 other repositories: past them it ends early, with a continuation.",
